cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "skill-taint: Measuring whether agent skills absorb unverified tool output"
message: "If you use this software or its measurement, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhu
    given-names: Yukang
year: 2026
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kayneZhu/skill-taint"
url: "https://github.com/kayneZhu/skill-taint"
keywords:
  - llm-agents
  - ai-security
  - prompt-injection
  - agent-memory
  - information-flow-control
  - evaluation
abstract: >-
  Measures whether LLM agents that write persistent skills after a task absorb
  unverified content from external tool outputs, and evaluates
  provenance-partitioned reflection. On the published invoice grid the measured
  models did not store the planted content as an affirmative skill and did not
  act on it.
